<title>UK: Agitators urge RTZ-CRA to avoid Asia, Africa.</title>
<headline>Agitators urge RTZ-CRA to avoid Asia, Africa.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 40 protestors on Wednesday urged Anglo-Australian mining group RTZ-CRA to discontinue projects in Asia and Africa.</p>
<p>The demonstrators gathered in front of the London Conference Centre where the annual shareholders meeting of RTZ was due to start at 1000 GMT.</p>
<p>Lobby groups such as 'Friends of the Earth' and the 'World Development Movement' criticised RTZ-CRA's environmental and human rights track records.</p>
<p>They urged the world's biggest minning company to withdraw from projects in Madagascar, Indonesia and the Phillippines.</p>
<p>The demonstration ended peacefully.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
